From 16671952fec4e5c2910b22bbb6c5b2b4ce0d4fa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: decklink-linux-anon
 <358323356+decklink-linux-anon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:49:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] decklink: External Video Output gamma (sRGB to Rec.709
 BT.1886 / As is)

Settings > Playback > External Video Output gamma (playback.transmitGamma):
srgbToBt1886 (default: sRGB EOTF to linear, re-encoded with gamma 1/2.4 for a
BT.1886 display; matched the Avid reference picture on the same TV) or asIs
(the sRGB values unchanged). Folded into the RGB to Y'CbCr tables, so it costs
nothing; switchable live (the current frame is resent).
decklink-test --gamma srgbToBt1886|asIs (default srgbToBt1886).
